+# capture-raw-mpp
+
+Encodes raw frames that another process publishes over a Unix socket, using Rockchip MPP. It offers the same outputs as `capture-v4l2-raw-mpp`, for when another process owns the camera.
+
+## Features
+
+- Accepts frames as a dma-buf fd (zero copy into the encoder) or as bytes on the socket
+- Hardware JPEG and H264 encoding (MPP), started on first use
+- Unix socket output for JPEG snapshots, MJPEG streams, H264 streams, and raw frames
+- Discards frames when no output has a client, and tells the publisher to stop sending them
+- Takes resolution from each frame; supports NV12 and NV21 without row padding
+
+## Protocol
+
+The publisher connects to `--input-sock` (`SOCK_STREAM`). A new publisher replaces the current one. Everything is in native byte order.
+
+Each frame starts with this header, sent as one message:
+
+```c
+struct frame_hdr {
+    uint32_t magic;   // 0x31465256
+    uint32_t type;    // 0: skip, 1: dma-buf, 2: data
+    uint32_t seq;     // echoed in the ack
+    uint32_t width;
+    uint32_t height;
+    uint32_t stride;  // bytes per line of the luma plane
+    uint32_t fourcc;  // V4L2 pixel format
+    uint32_t size;    // bytes used in the frame
+};
+```
+
+- `skip`: no frame, only lets the service reply while it does not want frames.
+- `dma-buf`: one fd is attached to the header with `SCM_RIGHTS`.
+- `data`: `size` bytes follow the header.
+
+The service answers every header once it has finished with the frame:
+
+```c
+struct frame_ack {
+    uint32_t seq;
+    uint32_t flags;   // bit 0: frames are wanted
+};
+```
+
+The publisher must not send another frame before the ack, and must not modify a dma-buf until then. Send `skip` while frames are not wanted. The service keeps references to dma-bufs it has seen, and drops them when the publisher disconnects.
